# SettlementOracle ZK — Core Conventions

## Source of Truth
- PRD: `docs/PRD.md`
- Architecture: `docs/architecture/mvp-system-overview.md`

## MVP Scope Guard
Before implementing any feature, verify it is in the MVP IN list in `AGENTS.md`.
If a request falls in the OUT list, stop and inform the user — do not implement.

## Security
- Never commit keypairs, `.env` files, or RPC URLs with embedded API keys
- All payout logic MUST execute on-chain via Anchor programs
- No off-chain fund transfers under any circumstance
- Use `solana-keygen` keypairs stored locally, referenced via env vars only

## Git
- Do NOT commit unless the user explicitly requests it
- Never force-push to main/master

## Naming
- Programs: `snake_case` (e.g., `escrow`, `payout`)
- TypeScript: `camelCase` functions, `PascalCase` types
- On-chain accounts: descriptive PDAs (e.g., `policy`, `escrow_vault`)

## Testing
- Every Anchor instruction must have at least one integration test
- Oracle connector must have unit tests for staleness/confidence edge cases
- Run `anchor test` before any devnet deploy
